-Sessions never expire.
+## Session expiry
+
+Each saved session records an `issued_at` timestamp. Sessions expire after
+`SESSION_TTL` (3600 seconds); `load_session` raises `SessionExpiredError` for an
+older session (or one without a valid `issued_at`). `purge_expired()` removes expired
+entries from the on-disk cache and is called on every restore.
+
+Resume blobs are base64-encoded JSON. Note that `issued_at` is not signed, so a client
+could forge it; sign blobs (e.g. HMAC) if clients are untrusted.
